  "narrative": "The constructed research-marker hypotheses are not supported. In signed form, H1, H2, and H3 have effect estimates near zero and 95% intervals that comfortably include null and lie well below the 0.15 dependency-unit meaningful threshold in the claimed direction; these are closed as uninformative for marker main effects. The marker-by-signature interactions H4-H6 are also null or weakly opposite in signed space, with intervals including zero; the arbitrary +0.75 SD signature threshold does not show meaningful dependency enhancement. \n\nThe genomic-loss predictors are more informative but require careful directional interpretation. For claims with direction -1, a positive signed estimate supports the original hypothesis that exposed samples have a more negative dependency_composite, i.e., stronger dependency. H9, SMARCA4 loss, has a very large positive signed estimate, 0.83, with a lower bound of about 0.77, far above the 0.15 threshold and robust to multiplicity in this discovery set. I accept H9 as a strong descriptive association: SMARCA4-loss samples have substantially stronger composite dependency in this dataset. This is not yet causal and may require technical confounding checks, so I registered Avana and non-Avana library stratifications of this effect. \n\nH7 and H11 are large but opposite to the claimed direction. Their signed estimates are negative, meaning the raw exposed-minus-comparator contrasts are positive: TP53 loss is associated with a roughly +0.42 unit more positive dependency_composite, and KEAP1 loss with roughly +0.83 unit more positive dependency_composite. Because more negative values mean stronger dependency, these are scientifically meaningful associations with weaker composite dependency, not stronger dependency. I therefore reject the original H7 and H11 directions while keeping them active to test reversed claims as refinements. \n\nH8, CDKN2A loss, supports the claimed stronger-dependency direction, but the signed point estimate is only 0.141, just below the 0.15 threshold, and the interval spans the threshold. It is statistically distinguishable from zero but not yet convincing as a meaningful effect-size finding. I mark it unresolved and request independent validation. H10 ARID1A loss and H12 KRAS mutation are not supported: ARID1A is small and opposite/uncertain, KRAS is essentially null. Overall, SMARCA4 loss is the clearest accepted discovery in the current evidence, while TP53 and KEAP1 losses generate promising reversed hypotheses and CDKN2A needs independent assessment before conclusion.",
  "research_notes": "Round 1 conclusion: constructed markers/signature interactions are null. Strong accepted finding: SMARCA4 loss associated with stronger composite dependency (signed estimate >0.75). Large opposite effects: TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss associated with weaker composite dependency; registered reversal proposals. CDKN2A loss is borderline above null but below meaningful threshold; requested validation for H8. Registered SMARCA4 library-stratified robustness checks by Avana/non-Avana to evaluate technical confounding. Next priorities: analyze reversals and library-stratified SMARCA4; assess H8 validation; consider broader technical confounders (screen batch, culture/media, growth/QC variables) before accepting any genomic association as stable.",
  "validate": "H8"
}

