  "narrative": "The new conditional PTEN analyses make the strongest case so far for PTEN loss as an additional dataset-level descriptive predictor, but they do not yet establish the global PTEN comparison with sufficient certainty. In the claimed stronger-dependency direction, PTEN loss within SMARCA4-intact/TP53-intact cells has a signed estimate of +0.261 with a 95% interval from +0.172 to +0.350. The lower bound exceeds the 0.15 composite-unit threshold, so I accept and close H66. PTEN loss within SMARCA4-intact/KEAP1-intact cells has a signed estimate of +0.255 with a lower bound +0.165, so I accept and close H68. PTEN loss within KEAP1-loss cells has a signed estimate of +0.378 with a lower bound +0.193, so I accept and close H65. These are important because they show that PTEN's apparent stronger-dependency association is not merely produced by the largest co-alteration strata: it remains above the meaningful threshold when SMARCA4 and TP53 are both intact, when SMARCA4 and KEAP1 are both intact, and even within the KEAP1-loss state where the global background is strongly shifted by KEAP1. They are still not causal or mechanistic statements.\n\nHowever, not every PTEN stratum is decisive. PTEN loss within SMARCA4-intact/TP53-intact but KEAP1-intact? specifically H67 has a signed estimate of +0.240, but its interval is +0.141 to +0.339, so the lower bound does not clear the 0.15 threshold. I therefore leave H67 unresolved and defer it; it is supportive but not decisive for a threshold-level effect. PTEN loss in the common adenocarcinoma subtype has a signed estimate of +0.207, but the lower bound is +0.097, below threshold, so I leave H69 unresolved and defer it. PTEN loss within SMARCA4-loss cells has a signed estimate of only +0.132 and an interval that includes negative values, and PTEN loss within TP53-loss cells has a signed estimate of +0.102 with a similarly wide interval. These co-altered strata are smaller and imprecise, and their direct evidence does not establish threshold-level effects, so I reject H61 and H63 as unsupported for those specific comparisons. This rejection is not proof of absence; it means the current evidence in those strata is too weak to support a meaningful claim.\n\nThe central remaining PTEN question is the global reversed claim H59. Its direct discovery estimate is +0.227 with a lower bound +0.131, just below the 0.15 threshold. The accepted conditional strata make a global PTEN association plausible, but conditional estimates are not direct validation of the global comparison, and multiple related PTEN comparisons raise multiplicity concerns. I therefore keep H59 unresolved and request independent validation of H59. If independent validation provides a global PTEN estimate with an interval whose lower bound clearly exceeds the threshold, I will accept the global PTEN claim. If it does not, the accepted evidence for PTEN will remain limited to the stronger conditional strata rather than a broad global predictor claim.\n\nThe SMARCA4-by-lineage interaction H55 is not supported in its claimed direction. The signed estimate is -0.211, interval -0.359 to -0.063. Because this claim's direction is negative, a positive signed estimate would support the claim; the observed negative estimate instead indicates evidence against the claimed negative interaction. The result is consistent with a positive interaction, but even that reversed effect is not yet established as exceeding the threshold because the reversed interval would be approximately +0.063 to +0.359. I therefore reject H55 as claimed and register a reversed-direction proposal parented to H55 so the positive interaction can be tested formally in future analyses. This remains a subtype descriptive finding, not evidence that lineage modifies the SMARCA4 effect causally or generally.\n\nThe broad genomic screen adds several useful negative results. ERBB2 amplification, PIK3CA mutation, and BRCA2 loss all have estimates and intervals far from the 0.15 threshold in the claimed directions, so H74, H75, and H76 are rejected and closed. MSI-high is the most unexpected new result. H77 claimed MSI-high with weaker dependency, but the signed estimate is -0.792 with an interval from -0.907 to -0.676. This is not only opposite the claimed direction but large in magnitude: it suggests MSI-high samples have much stronger composite dependency. I reject H77 as originally claimed, but because the opposite signal is large and precise enough to be scientifically interesting, I register a reversed MSI-high mean_difference proposal. This is explicitly data-driven and should not be treated as confirmatory until tested or independently validated; it is a candidate dataset-level descriptive association, not a causal or generalizable statement about MSI-high biology.\n\nOverall, the central descriptive conclusions are becoming clearer: SMARCA4 loss remains strongly associated with stronger dependency, TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss with weaker dependency, PTEN loss with stronger dependency in several clean or co-altered strata, and MSI-high with stronger dependency only as a newly proposed reversal from the negative H77 claim. Many other measured genomic or technical predictors remain unsupported. All statements remain within the supplied dataset and do not establish causality, single-gene knockout mechanisms, or broad biological generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 4 appraise updates: PTEN conditional strata provide the strongest new evidence. Accepted subgroup/descriptive PTEN claims: H66 SMARCA4-intact/TP53-intact, H68 SMARCA4-intact/KEAP1-intact, H65 KEAP1-loss state. These lower confidence bounds exceed 0.15 in the claimed stronger-dependency direction. H67 SMARCA4/KEAP1-intact? actually H67 lower 0.141, and H69 adenocarcinoma lower 0.097 remain unresolved/deferred. H61 SMARCA4-loss and H63 TP53-loss PTEN estimates are not supported and closed. Global PTEN H59 remains unresolved because its lower bound is 0.131; independent validation of H59 requested now.\n\nH55 SMARCA4-by-lineage interaction is rejected as originally claimed because the signed estimate is opposite the negative direction, though it suggests an uncertain positive interaction; reversed interaction proposal registered. Broad genomic negative results: H74 ERBB2 amp, H75 PIK3CA mutation, H76 BRCA2 loss rejected/closed. H77 MSI-high claimed weaker dependency is rejected because observed effect is large and opposite, consistent with MSI-high stronger dependency; reversed MSI-high proposal registered as data-driven follow-up.\n\nCurrent accepted central claims: H9 SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency; H13 TP53 loss weaker dependency; H14 KEAP1 loss weaker dependency; H65/H66/H68 PTEN loss stronger dependency in selected strata. H59 global PTEN pending validation. H78/reversed MSI-high and reversed SMARCA4-lineage interaction are new pending proposals. All conclusions are dataset-level descriptive associations; do not interpret as causal, single-gene knockout-specific, or generally biologically generalizable. Watch multiplicity especially around PTEN conditional strata and post-hoc direction reversals."
}

