  "narrative": "All estimates below are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction and are judged against the practical threshold of 0.15 composite dependency-score units. H62 reassesses PTEN loss within TP53-intact samples. The discovery estimate was +0.259 (95% CI +0.169 to +0.349), fully above threshold in the stronger-dependency direction, and independent validation was highly consistent in direction and magnitude: +0.255, although its very conservative lower bound (+0.099) falls just below threshold. Because the discovery evidence was strong and the validation is directionally and practically supportive, I maintain acceptance of H62 and close it. H61 reassesses PTEN loss within SMARCA4-loss samples. Discovery showed only +0.132 (95% CI -0.060 to +0.323), below threshold and crossing zero, while independent validation showed +0.426 but with lower bound +0.121, again not independently confirming the threshold. With small exposed cells and inconsistent threshold evidence, I cannot accept this context, but I also do not reject it as a precise null; it remains unresolved and is closed because additional near-boundary PTEN mining would not be informative. H14 reassesses global KEAP1 loss. Discovery was +0.832 (95% CI +0.766 to +0.897), and independent validation was +0.803 (95% CI +0.702 to +0.905). Both discovery and validation clear the threshold comfortably in the KEAP1-loss weaker-dependency direction, so I accept and close H14. This completes independent validation of the four central predictors: SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high are associated with stronger composite dependency, while TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss are associated with weaker composite dependency. The supported dataset-internal map is now mature and largely additive: SMARCA4-loss and MSI-high stronger-dependency associations are robust across many contexts including high chromosomal instability and high non-MSI mutation burden; TP53-loss and KEAP1-loss weaker-dependency associations are also robust across many contexts; PTEN loss is best supported conditionally in TP53-intact and MSI-nonhigh or clean central-intact backgrounds, with global and SMARCA4-loss-specific contexts remaining uncertain or near-threshold. Negative or nonmeaningful findings include constructed research markers and their signature interactions, most conventional driver or marker associations after broad screening, most effect-modifier interactions, and technical availability/library contrasts tested to date. No further voluntary validation requests remain, and central validation priorities are complete. The most informative next analyses are focused robustness tests of the validated central predictors in untested biological-state contexts, using top-quartile EMT, stemness, 8q24 copy gain, hypoxia, and IFN-gamma score subgroups restricted to MSI-nonhigh samples. If these central effects remain threshold-clearing there, the dataset-internal association map is even less sensitive to biological-state context; if they attenuate or cross zero, those contexts should be identified as boundaries. I avoided further near-threshold PTEN subgroup mining because the available evidence is inconsistent and likely underpowered. All conclusions remain descriptive, dataset-internal associations, not causal effects, not evidence of single-gene knockout mechanism specificity for the composite endpoint, and not evidence of external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 10 synthesis state: H14 global KEAP1 loss accepted and closed after validation: discovery +0.832 [0.766,0.897], validation +0.803 [0.702,0.905]. Central predictor validation complete: SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency, MSI-high stronger dependency, TP53 loss weaker dependency, KEAP1 loss weaker dependency, all with discovery and independent validation support. H62 PTEN loss in TP53-intact context remains accepted and closed: discovery +0.259 [0.169,0.349], validation +0.255 [0.099,0.411]; validation is directionally supportive though lower bound misses threshold. H61 PTEN loss in SMARCA4-loss context is now closed unresolved: discovery +0.132 [-0.060,0.323] did not clear threshold; validation +0.426 [0.121,0.731] is positive but does not independently clear threshold; avoid further near-threshold PTEN mining. PTEN map remains conditional strongest in TP53-intact/MSI-nonhigh and clean central-intact backgrounds. Global PTEN remains unresolved. Interaction evidence remains weak/rejected/deferred across central marker, lineage, QC, and MSI-by-TP53 variants. Next registered proposals test central robustness in top-quartile biological-state subgroups restricted to MSI-nonhigh: SMARCA4 loss in high EMT, high stemness, and high copy_number_8q24; TP53 loss in high hypoxia; KEAP1 loss in high IFN-gamma signature. If robust, biological-state context does not materially change central associations; if attenuated, those subgroups become important boundaries. No validation requests remain available."
