  "narrative": "No discovery assessments are due and no voluntary validation requests remain. The accepted central map is mature: SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high are associated with stronger composite dependency, whereas TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss are associated with weaker composite dependency. The active H136-H141 panel tests high-ploidy contexts. These new proposals add direct high-aneuploidy and proliferation-context effect-modification tests. The first three complete the central predictor x aneuploidy-score interaction panel among MSI-nonhigh samples, using the median as the top-half cutoff to keep cells adequately powered. The fourth tests whether the MSI-high association is modified by top-half aneuploidy. The last two test proliferation-rate modification for SMARCA4 loss among MSI-nonhigh samples and for MSI-high globally. For the interaction claims, a signed estimate above +0.15 means the named association is stronger in the top-half subgroup than in the complement, in the direction registered by each claim; near-zero or negative signed values would support robustness/additivity rather than a boundary. I anticipate mostly null modification because the central effects have already shown broad robustness, but a clear positive interaction would identify a scientifically important context boundary. These comparisons use measured, non-outcome-derived variables and remain descriptive associations in this dataset, not causal, gene-mechanistic, or externally generalizable claims.",
