  "narrative": "Final scientific report. All reported estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction; for direction -1, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has stronger dependency, whereas for direction +1, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has weaker dependency. The practical significance threshold is 0.15 composite dependency-score units. There are no assessments_due entries and no new validation releases to assess, and voluntary validation requests are exhausted. Therefore the controller-maintained accepted set remains unchanged, and I do not propose further same-dataset near-threshold mining. Supported dataset-internal central findings. First, SMARCA4 loss is strongly and robustly associated with stronger composite dependency: H9/R9 signed +0.833 with CI +0.767 to +0.898, independent validation R26 signed +0.803 with CI +0.699 to +0.907, and the effect remains above threshold across multiple strata including lower screen quality H166/R168 +0.853, higher screen quality H173/R175 +0.812, and above-median Cas9 score H177/R179 +0.716. Second, KEAP1 loss is strongly associated with weaker composite dependency: H14/R11 signed +0.832 with CI +0.766 to +0.897, validation R125 signed +0.803 with CI +0.702 to +0.905; related stratified evidence such as H168/R170 and H175/R177 is directionally consistent and threshold-clear. Third, MSI-high is associated with stronger composite dependency: H79/R52 signed +0.792 with CI +0.676 to +0.907 and validation R66 signed +0.826 with CI +0.635 to +1.017; robustness across controlled backgrounds, lower screen quality H169/R171, and higher screen quality H176/R178 supports the association as dataset-internal. Fourth, TP53 loss is associated with weaker composite dependency: H13/R7 signed +0.423 with CI +0.327 to +0.520, validation R39 signed +0.346 with CI +0.217 to +0.476; the effect is smaller than SMARCA4 and KEAP1 but directionally stable across many subgroups and technical strata. Context-dependent PTEN finding. PTEN loss is not established as a robust global predictor. The global direction -1 claim H59 remains unresolved because discovery R38 and validation R53 have point estimates supporting stronger dependency but uncertainty extending near or below the 0.15 threshold. In contrast, controlled TP53-intact, MSI-nonhigh backgrounds, often with SMARCA4-intact or additional high-quality QC/Cas9 conditioning, support a context-specific stronger-dependency association: examples include H62/R98 validated by R106, H80/R54, H97/R68 validated by R79, H110/R108 validated by R118, H149/R151, H162/R164, and the near-threshold high-Cas9 controlled contrast H182/R184 +0.282 with CI +0.157 to +0.407. Thus PTEN loss appears context-dependent in this dataset rather than uniformly above threshold. Negative findings. The constructed research markers are not scientifically meaningful predictors: marker D R1 -0.002 CI -0.061 to +0.058, marker E R2 +0.021 CI -0.039 to +0.080 with validation R80 +0.035 CI -0.052 to +0.121, marker F R3 +0.035 CI -0.025 to +0.094; their pre-specified signature interactions R4 to R6 are also null or subthreshold. Most other measured drivers are null or nonmeaningful: KRAS, STK11, MTAP, ARID1A, RB1, NF1, SMAD4, MYC amplification, EGFR amplification, BRAF V600E, ERBB2 amplification, PIK3CA mutation, BRCA2 loss, and APC mutation do not provide robust evidence for a 0.15-unit claimed association. CDKN2A loss is mostly rejected or unresolved, with near-threshold points but intervals compatible with subthreshold effects. Technical or experimental metadata also do not support meaningful associations: CRISPR Avana library, matched RNA/DNA status, media serum percentage, and sex contrasts are rejected. Interaction panels broadly argue against strong effect modification by lineage subtype, ploidy, aneuploidy, mutation burden, EMT, stemness, hypoxia, interferon signature, growth rate, Cas9 activity, screen quality, or PTEN-context interactions by more than the threshold; recent screen-quality and Cas9-score interactions for controlled PTEN contrasts R185 and R186 are null or subthreshold. Unresolved uncertainty. The main unresolved items are the exact PTEN context boundaries and near-threshold CDKN2A evidence. Some QC-conditioned, lineage, ploidy, aneuploidy, and mutation-burden stratified PTEN contrasts remain unresolved, and Cas9-score-conditioned analyses exclude observations missing Cas9 activity, which is a selection limitation. These unresolved items do not overturn the four central SMARCA4, TP53, KEAP1, and MSI-high findings, but they prevent a complete causal or mechanistic predictor map. Causality and generalizability. These results are descriptive associations among measured characteristics in one supplied observational dataset. The endpoint is a composite dependency score, not a single-gene knockout measurement, and predictors may be correlated without full multivariable adjustment. Independent validation within the supplied data strengthens the central contrasts but does not establish transportability, causality, mechanistic single-gene essentiality, or clinical generalizability. Most informative next analysis. I would not pursue more post hoc subgroup mining in this same dataset. The most informative next step is external pre-specified replication of the central contrasts: SMARCA4 loss versus intact, MSI-high versus MSI-nonhigh, TP53 loss versus intact, KEAP1 loss versus intact, and PTEN loss versus intact within TP53-intact/MSI-nonhigh and if feasible SMARCA4-intact backgrounds. A multivariable adjusted model including SMARCA4, TP53, KEAP1, MSI-high, PTEN, lineage, mutation burden or ploidy, and screen-quality variables, plus orthogonal dependency outcomes, would be more informative than further interactions. If only this dataset is available, the defensible conclusion is the robust central descriptive map with explicit PTEN context dependence and negative results for constructed markers, most drivers, technical covariates, and most interactions.",
  "research_notes": "Final report delivered. Do not reopen near-threshold same-dataset analyses. Central supported dataset-internal associations: SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency, MSI-high stronger dependency, TP53 loss weaker dependency, KEAP1 loss weaker dependency. PTEN loss is context-dependent, strongest in TP53-intact/MSI-nonhigh and controlled SMARCA4-intact backgrounds, but global PTEN remains unresolved. Markers D/E/F and most other driver or technical covariates are not meaningful. No further voluntary validation is possible or needed unless external data are provided. Next recommended analyses should be external pre-specified replication and multivariable adjustment, not additional post hoc interactions in this dataset."
