ors; and most effect-modification analyses are null or too imprecise, including screen_nnmd, culture type, adult status, and high-MYC amplification for SMARCA4. Unresolved uncertainty: global PTEN remains unresolved because point estimates can exceed threshold while interval lower bounds do not; PTEN in high-MYC context remains pending via H230 after deferring H229 because its cells are small and precision is poor; several PTEN strata with smaller cells or interval lower bounds near threshold remain unresolved; TP53 in Ky-library screens, TP53 within MSI-high strata, TP53-by-KEAP1 interaction, and some culture/age/lineage boundaries remain uncertain. The most informative next analysis within the supplied dataset is to analyze H230, the less restrictive adult TP53-intact MSI-nonhigh high-MYC PTEN-loss contrast. If H230 clears the 0.15 threshold, the PTEN-loss stronger-dependency association extends to the high-MYC background; if it does not, high-MYC PTEN should remain unresolved and the final PTEN conclusion should stay context-dependent. For external validation, the highest-value design is a prespecified replication of the four central associations using orthogonal dependency endpoints, with adjustment for lineage, screen quality, Cas9 activity, mutation burden/ploidy, QC completeness, and library context. All conclusions are observational associations in the supplied dataset and do not establish causality, single-gene essentiality, clinical transportability, or generalizability.",
